35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, this is scary! No freeze window means we can’t stop the floor. The 2021 trial failed fast. We need a system that works with our old scanners!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the floor is critical, but my data shows the real trap. Bundled prices stay flat, but add-ons climb yearly. We are buying a subscription to surprise bills.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, surprise bills are manageable. Unowned outages are not. My data confirms support is scattered across four suppliers, leaving failures unaddressed for days.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, four suppliers? That’s chaos! My data shows the dispatch tool skipped upgrades for years, and the 2018 pay move broke for a whole year. We need one clear owner!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your findings confirm my fear. Two administrators retire this year, and the last posting stayed open eleven months. We are losing the minds that hold this together.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, one owner is vital! But my yard scanners are old. If the new system can’t talk to them, we’re stuck. We need compatibility first!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, one owner is a start, but my board minutes show capital gets cut while operating costs pass silently. We are funding the bleed, not the cure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, one owner is necessary, but insufficient. My data shows the administrators who understand the system are leaving. We need a vendor who can absorb that institutional loss.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! The 2018 mess proves outside work needs repair. We need a vendor who stays to fix the cracks, not just install the shiny new thing!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right. The hands are leaving, and the supervisors already dropped the last training. We must choose a vendor who teaches the crews, not just the software.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, teaching the crews is key! But my scanners are old. If the new system can’t talk to them, training is useless. We need hardware compatibility!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, hardware compatibility is a one-time cost. My data shows the recurring operating lines are the silent killer. We must price the lifetime bleed, not just the initial handshake.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, the bleed is real, but unowned failure is fatal. I need a vendor who absorbs the administrative vacuum, not just one who cuts costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, the bleed is real, but the 2018 mess shows who fixes it matters more! We need a partner who stays to repair the cracks, not just install the shiny new thing!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right. A partner who stays is essential. But I worry the crews will forget again. We need a vendor who respects the human rhythm, not just the code.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, I hear you on the costs. But if the scanners can’t talk to the new system, we’re dead in the water. Compatibility is my non-negotiable!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, compatibility is a line item. My data shows the recurring operating lines are the silent killer. We must price the lifetime bleed, not just the initial handshake.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, compatibility is a feature. Accountability is a structure. I need a vendor who owns the failure, not just the hardware.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, scanners are just tools! The real danger is the system aging in place. We need a vendor who keeps it fresh, not one who lets it rot!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the scanners are vital, but the hands that operate them are the true foundation. We must choose a vendor who respects the human rhythm, not just the code.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
